# M5 red team (docs/redteam/m5-movss-db.md lists what held): one ring-3
# thread runs 80 probes (user/root/src/redteam/probes.rs), each a
# privileged or faulting instruction sequence, with the root task as its
# fault handler, which resumes it past each probe with TCB_WriteRegisters.
# Every probe must end in the fault docs/abi.md names, with IOPL 0, and the
# kernel must not panic: int n for the NMI, #DF, #MC, timer and device
# vectors, int1, sysenter, sysexit, sysretq, privileged instructions, far
# returns and iretq to every GDT selector, IOPL 3 by popfq and iretq, NT,
# kernel and non-canonical addresses, TF and AC across syscall, a pending
# x87 #MF across a thread switch, bad XSAVE headers, a syscall with a
# non-canonical or kernel RSP (which returns RSP 0), and unknown numbers.
# QEMU 8.2 TCG differs from hardware in four ways the probes accept: #PF
# for non-canonical addresses, a SMAP #PF for retfq and iretq in ring 3, #UD
# for int1, and no MXCSR reserved-bit check or #XM.
cmdline: test=redteam-exceptions
exit: success
expect: microL4 kernel
expect: root: cmdline "test=redteam-exceptions"
expect: redteam: exceptions: 80 probes in thread
expect: probe 1 (int 2, the NMI vector): label 3, 0xd/0x12
expect: probe 3 (int 18, the #MC vector): label 3, 0xd/0x92
expect: probe 51 (popfq asking for IOPL 3, then cli): label 3, 0xd/0x0
expect: probe 61 (TF set across syscall (Yield)): label 3, 0x1/0x0
expect: probe 65 (AC and DF set, a misaligned read, Yield, then int3): label 3, 0x3/0x0
expect: probe 67 (x87 #MF delivered by fwait): label 3, 0x10/0x0
expect: entry: warning: RSP 0x800000000000 at or above 2^47 exits as 0
expect: probe 74 (syscall (Yield) with a non-canonical RSP, then int3): label 3, 0x3/0x0
expect: rsp 0x0
expect: probe 79 (syscall number 2^64 - 1): label 2, 0xffffffffffffffff/0x0
expect: redteam: exceptions: all 80 probes ended in their own fault
expect: TEST PASS
expect: DEBUG HALT 0 from TCB
